==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla-pro|sh}} {{m|sla-pro|*grana}} (cognate with dialectal or obsolete Bulgarian {{term|sc=Cyrl|гран|lang=bg}}/{{term|sc=Cyrl|гранка|lang=bg}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|sh}}, cognate with German {{term|Granne||awn|lang=de}}, Old English {{term|granu||moustache|lang=ang}} and Old Norse {{term|grǫn||a pine tree|lang=non}} ( > Danish {{term|gran||spruce|lang=da}}). Compare Old Norse {{term|grein||branch|lang=non}} ( > Danish {{term|gren|lang=da}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡrǎːna/|lang=sh}}
* {{hyphenation|gra|na|lang=sh}}
* {{rhymes|ǎːna|lang=sh}}

===Noun===
{{sh-noun|g=f|head=grána|r|грана|гра́на}}

# [[branch]]
#: {{usex|slomljena grana|t=a broken branch|lang=sh|inline=1}}
#: {{usex|bolje vrabac u ruci nego golub na grani|t=[[a bird in the hand is worth two in the bush]]|lang=sh|inline=1}}
# [[field]], [[branch]]
#: {{usex|grana znanosti/nauke|t=a branch of science|lang=sh|inline=1}}
